<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Quaker Oats cut to reduce.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Quaker Oats cut to reduce.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>SBC Warburg analyst Chris Jakubik said Friday he reduced his rating on Quaker Oats Co to reduce from hold on valuation.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Recent outperformance has brought the stock price uncomfortably close to our estimate for the company's private market value,&quot; Jakubik said.</p>
<p>-- He also raised earnings estimates for Quaker to $1.75 frm $1.60 a share for 1997 and to $2.15 from $2.00 for 1998. Earnings estimates were raised to reflect disposition of Quaker's Snapple beverage business and use of the proceeds.</p>
<p>-- Quaker shares were unchanged at 44-3/8.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
